.TH SUM 1.SH NAMEsum \- print a checksum and block count.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsum\fR[file ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBsum\fRis GNU sum, from the textutils.  For each named file it prints a 16-bitchecksum, the size in 1024-byte blocks, and the name.  With no file itreads the standard input and prints no name..PPThe checksum is the BSD algorithm, so a file that gives the same pair ofnumbers here and on another machine has almost certainly crossed intact.This build takes no options: an argument beginning with a dash is takenas a file name..SH EXAMPLES.nfsum notes               checksum, blocks and the namesum < notes             checksum and blocks only.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOwc